### How do automated tests make refactoring safe?

Unit tests cover business logic with meaningful assertions. Integration tests verify components work together. The tests are the safety net that lets you refactor with confidence -- if something breaks, a test catches it immediately.

```java
package com.bank.loans;

import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import java.math.BigDecimal;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

class EmiCalculatorTest {

    private final EmiCalculator calculator = new EmiCalculator();

    @Test
    void calculateEmi_standardHomeLoan() {
        BigDecimal emi = calculator.calculateMonthlyEmi(
            new BigDecimal("5000000.00"),
            new BigDecimal("8.50"),
            240
        );
        assertEquals(new BigDecimal("43391.28"), emi);
    }

    @Test
    void calculateEmi_zeroInterest() {
        BigDecimal emi = calculator.calculateMonthlyEmi(
            new BigDecimal("1200000.00"),
            BigDecimal.ZERO,
            12
        );
        assertEquals(new BigDecimal("100000.00"), emi);
    }

    @Test
    void calculateEmi_singleMonth() {
        BigDecimal emi = calculator.calculateMonthlyEmi(
            new BigDecimal("100000.00"),
            new BigDecimal("12.00"),
            1
        );
        assertEquals(new BigDecimal("101000.00"), emi);
    }
}
```

