### How is refactoring done continuously?

Refactoring is continuous, not a one-off project. Follow the rule of leaving code a little cleaner than you found it, always backed by tests so behavior is preserved.

```java
// Before: found during a feature addition
public void process(String type, BigDecimal amount) {
    if (type.equals("NEFT")) {
        // 20 lines of NEFT logic
    } else if (type.equals("RTGS")) {
        // 20 lines of RTGS logic
    } else if (type.equals("UPI")) {
        // 20 lines of UPI logic
    }
}

// After: extract strategy, tests still pass
public interface TransferStrategy {
    void execute(BigDecimal amount);
}

public void process(String type, BigDecimal amount) {
    TransferStrategy strategy = strategyFactory.get(type);
    strategy.execute(amount);
}
```

### What should a senior engineer know?

Quality is not a phase at the end -- it is a set of fast feedback loops. The compiler, the tests, the linter, the reviewer, and the pipeline each catch problems at progressively later stages. The cost of a defect grows the later it is found, and in banking a defect found in production costs real money and trust.
